codex
I found one material CI identity flaw despite the green composite evidence: the workflow accepts `candidate_ref` and `candidate_root` simultaneously, then verifies/checks out the ref but runs and records the root while still stamping the supplied ref as `candidate_revision`. That can produce candidate evidence whose revision and measured bytes are unrelated, violating the exact-identity/anti-impersonation acceptance criterion. I’m documenting this as ordinary rework (not a blocker) with the minimal remediation and the otherwise-green evidence.
